/P 53 0 R
/E (The first instruction calculates the addition of x and y and stores the result in t1. The second instruction takes the value stored in t1 and multiplies it by z, giving the result in t2. The third instruction divides t2 by w and stores the result in t3. Finally, the fourth instruction subtracts p from t3 and stores the final result in t4.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
