/P 54 0 R
/E (Alignment is another important factor. Some processors require certain data types to start at particular memory boundaries. For example, a double may need an address aligned to an 8-byte boundary. If a char is placed immediately before a double, the compiler may insert unused padding bytes so that the double starts at the correct boundary.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
